From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nydal91 <nydal91@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:29:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/18] Add GitHub Actions workflow for the ARM64EC build

Build on pushes to master and on demand, and upload the full and core
packages as artifacts. Pushing an arm64ec-* tag also publishes them as a
release.

Track arm64ec/libs because a clean runner cannot rebuild them: the FSR
fork sources are not recorded anywhere in the repository. This matches
how upstream tracks its x64 libraries in OptiScaler/library.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A9WqnwGsLAcGJXd49N2pes
---
 arm64ec/.gitignore             | 6 +++++-
 arm64ec/docs/proton-arm64ec.md | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arm64ec/.gitignore b/arm64ec/.gitignore
index 18dfa2b..eae63aa 100644
--- a/arm64ec/.gitignore
+++ b/arm64ec/.gitignore
@@ -1,5 +1,9 @@
 # Build artifacts (large) — the scripts and docs stay tracked.
-/libs/
 /Release/
 /ReleaseDebug/
+/zip/
 /*.zip
+
+# Prebuilt dependency libraries are tracked so CI can link without rebuilding
+# them (the root .gitignore excludes *.lib).
+!/libs/**
diff --git a/arm64ec/docs/proton-arm64ec.md b/arm64ec/docs/proton-arm64ec.md
index cce57e7..02b2fe2 100644
--- a/arm64ec/docs/proton-arm64ec.md
+++ b/arm64ec/docs/proton-arm64ec.md
@@ -84,3 +84,7 @@ Then build on Windows with Visual Studio 2022 and the ARM64EC tools:
 ```
 powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File arm64ec\build-optiscaler.ps1
 ```
+
+`arm64ec/libs` holds prebuilt dependency libraries, so add `-SkipDeps` to reuse
+them. The `Build ARM64EC` GitHub Actions workflow does this on every push to
+`master`. Pushing an `arm64ec-*` tag also publishes a release.
